# Manual Identity recovery. See ACCOUNT-LIFECYCLE.md. Run one request at a time.
# Start signed out (auth.http A7/A8 if necessary), retaining cookies.
# Use a disposable Development account; never commit real values.
# All account requests share 20/minute/source IP. A 429 means wait before continuing.
@baseUrl = https://localhost:7240
@csrfToken = REPLACE_WITH_CURRENT_ANONYMOUS_CSRF_TOKEN
@email = REPLACE_WITH_CONFIRMED_LOCAL_EMAIL
@newPassword = REPLACE_WITH_NEW_LOCAL_PASSWORD
@resetToken = REPLACE_FROM_RESET_PASSWORD_MAIL_PAYLOAD
@userId = REPLACE_FROM_CONFIRM_EMAIL_MAIL_PAYLOAD
@confirmationToken = REPLACE_FROM_CONFIRM_EMAIL_MAIL_PAYLOAD
@unconfirmedEmail = REPLACE_WITH_UNCONFIRMED_LOCAL_EMAIL

### R1. Get anonymous CSRF; copy JSON token into csrfToken, retain cookie
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/csrf

### R2. Request password reset
# 202 generically; confirmed active account creates purpose=reset-password JSON in
# src/hosts/Atlas.Api/development-mail/ (or configured override). No token in response.
# Copy token from that private file into resetToken; do not use the confirmation token.
# 503 outside Development until production delivery exists.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "email": "{{email}}" }

### R3. Apply new password
# 204 success, 400 generic failure. Does not sign in, clear lockout or reactivate a profile.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "email": "{{email}}", "token": "{{resetToken}}", "newPassword": "{{newPassword}}" }

### R4. Replay the consumed token from R3
# After successful R3, expect 400. Keep the same token; do not request a replacement first.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "email": "{{email}}", "token": "{{resetToken}}", "newPassword": "{{newPassword}}" }

### R5. Login with the new password
# 204. Then run R6 and use the authenticated token for subsequent writes.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{newPassword}}" }

### R6. Refresh CSRF after login; copy returned token before any writes
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/csrf

### R7. Verify authenticated session (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/session

### R8. Logout (204); requires the authenticated csrfToken from R6
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

### R9. Refresh anonymous CSRF for the separate resend scenario
# Copy JSON token into csrfToken. Create a separate unconfirmed user with auth.http first.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/csrf

### R10. Resend confirmation for that unconfirmed user
# 202 generically; eligible account creates purpose=confirm-email payload.
# Copy its userId/token into the separate confirmation variables above.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/resend-confirmation
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "email": "{{unconfirmedEmail}}" }

### R11. Confirm the unconfirmed account (204); does not log in
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/confirm-email
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "userId": "{{userId}}", "token": "{{confirmationToken}}" }
